 "notes": [
  {
   "h": "Where was Makkedah?",
   "p": [
    "Makkedah lay in the Shephelah, the low hills between the Judean hill country and the coastal plain, near Azekah and on the way south toward Lachish and Eglon. Its site is not certain. The map follows OpenBible.info's leading suggestion, Khirbet el-Qom, with only modest confidence."
   ],
   "alternates": true
  },
  {
   "h": "About the routes",
   "p": [
    "The text says only that Israel struck the fleeing army \"from behind\" so that few reached their cities (vv. 19–20), and that the army returned to the camp at Makkedah (v. 21). The arrows toward the five cities show that direction of escape, not recorded roads."
   ]
  }
 ]
